WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.275
So, four asks.

2
00:00:01.275 --> 00:00:04.366
Adopt this book's
Conditional Access library

3
00:00:04.366 --> 00:00:07.375
and wave plan as the
agency's access baseline.

4
00:00:07.375 --> 00:00:11.724
End standing privilege: every
administrator role eligible through PIM,

5
00:00:11.724 --> 00:00:16.000
with two governed break-glass accounts
as the only standing exception.

6
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.198
Separate deciding from
executing: name the owners,

7
00:00:19.198 --> 00:00:23.537
scope the help desk role, and stand
up the identity governance office.

8
00:00:23.537 --> 00:00:26.677
And manage access as code,
with version control,

9
00:00:26.677 --> 00:00:30.863
review and drift monitoring,
keeping the evidence from day one.

10
00:00:30.863 --> 00:00:35.163
In Zero Trust, every access
decision is a policy decision.

11
00:00:35.163 --> 00:00:37.632
Writing that policy down, testing it,

12
00:00:37.632 --> 00:00:42.075
and proving it ran is how an agency
knows who can reach what, and why.

13
00:00:42.075 --> 00:00:45.414
Access and Privilege has the
full library and settings,

14
00:00:45.414 --> 00:00:49.260
with every external claim footnoted,
and Devices and Endpoints

15
00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:52.962
covers the device compliance
that Conditional Access reads.

16
00:00:52.962 --> 00:00:53.780
Thank you.
